"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h2>Identified States</h2>\n<p>✅ State analysis complete</p>\n<p>This formal analysis identifies the states of a <strong>User Authentication Flow</strong> within a Web Application Security context. The model follows a finite state machine (FSM) approach, accounting for security protocols like Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) and account lockout policies.</p>\n<hr />\n<h3>1. State: Logged Out</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> The default state where no user identity is associated with the current session.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Initial / Normal</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> No valid Session Token exists in the client storage or server-side session cache.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Application launch; User explicitly clicks &quot;Logout&quot;; Session Token is revoked by the server.</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong> User provides a username/identifier to begin the authentication process.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. State: Validating Primary Credentials</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> A transient state where the system is verifying the provided username and password against the identity provider.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Normal (Transient)</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> The system is actively processing a cryptographic hash comparison.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> User submits the login form with primary credentials.</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Success:</strong> Credentials match (Transition to <em>MFA Challenge Pending</em> or <em>Logged In</em>).</li>\n<li><strong>Failure:</strong> Credentials do not match (Transition to <em>Authentication Failed</em>).</li>\n<li><strong>System Error:</strong> Database or Identity Provider is unreachable (Transition to <em>Service Unavailable</em>).</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. State: MFA Challenge Pending</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> Primary credentials are correct, but the system requires a second factor (TOTP, SMS, WebAuthn).</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Normal</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> Primary identity is verified; Session is in a &quot;Partial Auth&quot; state (restricted access).</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Primary credentials validated AND MFA is enabled for the account.</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Success:</strong> Valid MFA token provided.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure:</strong> Invalid MFA token or maximum MFA attempts reached.</li>\n<li><strong>Timeout:</strong> User fails to provide MFA within the allowed window.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4. State: Logged In</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> The user is fully authenticated and authorized to access protected resources.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Normal (Stable)</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> A valid, non-expired Session Token is held by the client; User identity is bound to the session.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Successful validation of all required authentication factors.</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong> User logs out; Session expires (idle or absolute); Account is suspended by an admin; Password is changed from another device.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>5. State: Authentication Failed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> The attempt to authenticate was rejected due to incorrect information.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Error</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> No session is created; An increment is added to the &quot;Failed Attempt&quot; counter for the specific IP or User ID.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Incorrect password or incorrect MFA token provided.</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong> User attempts to login again; User initiates &quot;Forgot Password&quot; flow.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>6. State: Account Locked</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> The account is temporarily or permanently barred from authentication attempts due to security policy violations.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Error / Security</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> The <code>is_locked</code> flag is true in the user database; Authentication attempts are rejected immediately without credential validation.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Failed attempt counter exceeds the defined threshold (e.g., 5 failed tries).</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong> Lockout timer expires (Cool-down); Administrative unlock; Successful &quot;Unlock Account&quot; flow via email verification.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>7. State: Password Reset Required</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> The user has successfully authenticated, but the system requires a password change before granting full access.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Normal (Intermediary)</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> Identity is verified; Access is restricted strictly to the &quot;Change Password&quot; functionality.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Password has expired (Policy); Admin flagged the account for a forced reset (e.g., after a data breach).</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong> Successful password update (Transitions to <em>Logged In</em>); User logs out.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>8. State: Session Expired</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> A previously valid session has become invalid due to time constraints.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Error / Transient</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> The Session Token exists but the server-side timestamp exceeds the <code>max_age</code> or <code>idle_timeout</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Current Time &gt; (Last Activity + Idle Timeout) OR Current Time &gt; (Session Start + Absolute Timeout).</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong> Automatic redirection to <em>Logged Out</em> state.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>9. State: Account Suspended</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Description:</strong> The account is disabled by system administrators, often for Terms of Service violations or suspicious activity.</li>\n<li><strong>Type:</strong> Final (for the user session)</li>\n<li><strong>Invariants:</strong> User record is marked as <code>inactive</code> or <code>suspended</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Entry Conditions:</strong> Manual administrative action; Automated fraud detection trigger.</li>\n<li><strong>Exit Conditions:</strong> Manual administrative reinstatement.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<h3>Summary Table for Formal Modeling</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th align=\"left\">State Name</th><th align=\"left\">Type</th><th align=\"left\">Primary Invariant</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Initial</td><td align=\"left\"><code>Session == Null</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Transient</td><td align=\"left\"><code>Processing == True</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>MFA Pending</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Normal</td><td align=\"left\"><code>PrimaryAuth == True &amp;&amp; SecondaryAuth == False</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged In</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Stable</td><td align=\"left\"><code>Session.isValid == True</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Auth Failed</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Error</td><td align=\"left\"><code>RetryCount++</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Account Locked</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Security</td><td align=\"left\"><code>AllowLogin == False</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Reset Required</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Intermediary</td><td align=\"left\"><code>Scope == &quot;PasswordChangeOnly&quot;</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Session Expired</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Error</td><td align=\"left\"><code>Token.expiry &lt; CurrentTime</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Suspended</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Terminal</td><td align=\"left\"><code>User.status == &quot;Disabled&quot;</code></td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div></div><div><div class=\"spinner-border\" role=\"status\"><span class=\"sr-only\">Loading...</span></div></div>"